{"bundle_format":1,"conflicts":[{"between":["architecture 3.5"],"decision":"Reminder days. BA-6 (6.1) and 6.2 item 6 ask for 2 business days. Section 3.5 says 3. The architecture document is the ground truth and an earlier section wins over the business analyst note, so use 3. The next document version should settle the number. Keep it in one constant.","recorded":null},{"between":["architecture 4.2"],"decision":"The email may hold amounts and comments, but the event, the queue and the logs must not (R4 of 8.1, GOV-2.6). An address never goes into an event or an audit record (GOV-2.3). The worker uses `recipient_id` and never picks the recipient. Build the email at send time and keep nothing.","recorded":null}],"content_sha256":"814895232edef5724fdeea268e48a42f8b53b7ddfc8d4ed78bea910990b82a20","downstream":{"code":true,"evidence":"synthetic-only","issues":false,"tests":true},"extensions":{},"obligations":[{"heading":"Functional requirements","section":"2.1","sha256":"08161b91dd0e23c30658755149be8a0df456ae56972af19f900c720aca252ff0","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"Data model","section":"3.3","sha256":"d60f0970a2509aad0b9286733547d3f79e70752450ad3a95421bbf688bff529b","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"Report lifecycle","section":"3.4","sha256":"0e09d60151206062a001fed628eda80598d3fa186133640424e16352b5e91c89","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"Routing","section":"3.5","sha256":"8db9241b604c82b80e06ff5698ca67b5c7f79ee2a75844ef7322198fa6c8fd8e","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"GOV-1 Approval limits and separation of duties","section":"4.1","sha256":"ab60fab5f12f33cd79b8378e12ee82f19ec7c226873c805a016b73bddae7dfc1","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"GOV-2 Audit and retention","section":"4.2","sha256":"0aedc87487d48c1242e2a8f3c7577fb101ad069fdf4290ae71ed31ac1401b9f5","source":"architecture","version":"0.3"},{"heading":"DS-1 Delivery standard","section":"5.1","sha256":"6eb56449ea